ARTIFACT SUMMARY (native parity port of web/src/components/feedback/FeedbackModal.tsx)

Architecture — the 4-file modal-surface pattern (mirrors the IncidentForm write-only-modal precedent):
  FeedbackModal.Model.cs      (WinUI-free) FeedbackCategory enum + wire mapping; FeedbackErrorReport /
                              FeedbackContext / FeedbackSubmitRequest / FeedbackSubmitOutcome / toast
                              records (snake_case JSON matching the Go feedbackRequest); FeedbackModalRegistration
                              (slug, bounds, i18n keys); FeedbackModalProjection (options, zod-equivalent
                              validation, console-tail slicing, payload assembly); FeedbackModalDiagnostics.
  FeedbackModal.Source.cs     (WinUI-free) IFeedbackSubmitSource + FeedbackSubmitSource over IApiClient
                              (post_api_v1_feedback) — the useSubmitFeedback adapter; IFeedbackContextSource +
                              FeedbackContextSource (useLocation + IPushEnvironment + diagnostics ring) +
                              StaticFeedbackContextSource (headless); IFeedbackDiagnosticsLog +
                              InMemoryFeedbackDiagnosticsLog (the errorReporter ring + console-tail analogue).
  FeedbackModal.ViewModel.cs  (WinUI-free) INotifyPropertyChanged state holder: category/title/body + the two
                              consent toggles, zod-equivalent validation behind the submit gate, context capture
                              on open, submit flow (pending/success-and-close/inline+toast failure), diagnostics.
  FeedbackModal.cs            (WinUI 3 view) TsModal-hosted form: TsSelect category, TsInput title, TsTextarea
                              details, TsGlassPanel auto-attached-context panel (Page / App version / System rows
                              + the two TsToggles with HelperText), inline error InfoBar, Send/Cancel. Marshals
                              view-model changes onto the dispatcher; never performs HTTP.

Data sources (bound via the shared P1/S8 state-holder seams — no direct HTTP from the view):
  useSubmitFeedback -> IFeedbackSubmitSource (POST /feedback via the generated contract client)
  useFeedback       -> same submit hook file (FeedbackSubmitSource)
  useLocation       -> FeedbackContextSource current-route provider (shell NavigationHistory.Current; "/" default)
  useTranslation    -> ILocalizer (P1/S10 i18n facade)

States (all render — write-only modal, so NO loading/stale/offline read branch, exactly like the web source):
  editable form (always) ; per-field validation errors (title 5..120, details 20..4000, on blur + on submit) ;
  submitting (busy "Submitting…" primary, disabled) ; submit failure (inline assertive InfoBar, modal stays
  open, Send re-enabled = retry) ; success (toast + close) ; "empty" context -> friendly "unknown" fallback for
  a missing app version / runtime, never a blank box.

i18n (every web key kept; resolved through the P1/S10 ILocalizer; no English literals in view/view-model):
  feedback.title, feedback.category.{bug,feature,other}, feedback.form.category.label,
  feedback.form.title.{label,placeholder}, feedback.form.body.{label,placeholder}, feedback.context.{title,page,
  appVersion,userAgent,unknown}, feedback.form.{includeErrors,includeErrorsHint,includeConsole,includeConsoleHint},
  feedback.submitError, common.cancel, feedback.form.{submit,submitting}, toast.feedback.submit.{success,error}.
  DELIBERATE, DOCUMENTED idiom adaptation (key kept, English fallback adapted for a native Windows app):
    feedback.context.userAgent  "Browser" -> "System" (captured value is the OS/app/locale runtime descriptor)
    feedback.form.includeConsole "console messages" -> "log messages" (native diagnostics tail is an app log)

Accessibility: every interactive element carries a Narrator name (its i18n label); validation/error regions are
assertive live regions; no bespoke motion (reduced-motion honoured by construction). Asserted by the a11y label test.

Telemetry: FeedbackModalDiagnostics emits "view.opened slug=FeedbackModal" on open and
"feedback.submitted slug=FeedbackModal" on success — PII-safe (never the title/body/route/runtime/errors/tail),
per the P1/S11 diagnostics contract.

Pre-existing repo fix REQUIRED for a runnable gate (documented; not silent): the test project
apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj was corrupted at baseline into TWO <Project> roots
(MSB4025 "multiple root elements") by its documented .gitattributes merge=union failure mode, so the baseline
`dotnet build sln` and `dotnet test sln` could not even load it. Per the file's own INVARIANT comment it was
re-consolidated into ONE canonical root (the deduplicated union of the 830 existing Compile links — verified
zero conflicting links — plus the 3 new FeedbackModal ModalsDialogs links). All 17,234 headless tests pass,
confirming the union is intact.

